  "worked_solution": "To get $a$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y={x}^{3}+8.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+8 & =y \\\\ {x}^{3}+8 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-8 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2.$",
